[Music]  the release of the Last Guardian on ps4  will be the culmination of almost a  decade of development a process that  began all the way back in 2007 that's a  long time to be hearing very little and  seeing even less about a game that is  one of the most anticipated titles this  year or indeed ever so if you want to  find out why the hype is so high for  this white whale of a video game why  team ICO's previous games Shadow of the  Colossus and ICO are consistently cited  as some of the best games of all time  and how an unanticipated player reaction  to a feature in a previous game led for  me to await up to the central concept of  the Last Guardian stay tuned as we take  a look back at the history and legacy of  Team Ico in 1997 Fumito a waiter  joined Sony Computer Entertainment as a  first party game designer having  previously worked on enemy zero on the  Sega Saturn he began working on an  animation to convey the idea for his  first game inspired by elements of  Prince of Persia another world and  lemmings the core idea revolved around a  simple boy-meets-girl story where the  two main characters would form an  emotional bond without communicating  that animation and idea would become the  team's first game and namesake Iko Iko  sometimes pronounced eco tells the story  of ICO a boy born with bullhorns who is  locked away in a stone coffin in an  abandoned fortress when he comes of age  while trying to escape ICO stumbles  across Yoda a young girl in an equally  tragic situation her mother the Queen  intends to sacrifice yatta to extend her  own life Eiko decides to help your to  escape and the two set out together to  find a way out of the fortress  Aiko's gameplay revolves around puzzle  platforming and traversal with the  player directly controlling Eiko  unfortunately Yoda isn't nearly as  mobile or adventurous as Eiko which  showcases echos most iconic gameplay  mechanic by holding r1 players can take  Yoda by the hand and lead her through  obstacles and away from danger  puzzles are never overly difficult or  obtuse but the necessity to help you or  to overcome them serves to strengthen  the emotional bond between the two  likewise combat is a simple one-button  affair that serves only to rescue Yoda  as the game's enemies attempt to kidnap  her and dragged her into shadowy  vortexes Eiko was designed using the  process  of as a waiter himself describes it  subtracting design wherein elements were  removed if they impacted the design  goals of the team this resulted in many  elements that would uniquely distinguish  ICO including a lack of heads-up display  and interface and it's singular shadowy  figure enemy type originally the game  focused on ICO attempting to return the  order to her room in the fortress after  she is kidnapped by horned warriors but  a waiter deemed the warriors to  graphically intensive for the engine so  they were replaced with the final games  shadow creatures after changing release  platforms from the original PlayStation  2 the PlayStation 2 in addition to four  years of development ICO was released in  North America on September 24 2001 the  game was a critical success with  GameSpot's miguel lopez awarding it an  8.5 and concluding ICO serves as a  strong testament to the potential of  video game aesthetics and boldly asserts  that a strong production can indeed a  driver game when it's coupled with solid  play mechanics critical success didn't  translate into commercial success  however with ICO selling less than  300,000 copies in North America as of  2009 these low sales and its sparse  presence at retail helped to create a  cult status around ICO that has  continued to this day  several factors have been blamed for  Aiko's disappointing sales in North  America while Fumito Widow drew the  European and Japanese cover art himself  North American copies were sold with a  generic rushed cover that has been  called the worst video game cover ever  made the American version also liked  several unlockable bonuses including a  two-player mode and translation for  yours dialogue a waiter has also said  that his insistence on subtracting  design may have taken too much out of  the game something he vowed to minimize  on his next project Shadow of the  Colossus  [Music]  Team Ico began work on Shadow of the  Colossus in 2002 under the name Nikko a  way to conceive the game to challenge  the perceived idea of what a video game  boss could be as such 16 colossi are the  only enemies in the game each with a  unique arena and behavioral pattern for  players to overcome Shadow of the  Colossus tells the story of wander a  young man on a quest to resurrect a  young woman travelling with his only  companion a horse named agro wander  enters the Forbidden Land to make a  bargain with an entity known as doorman  doorman is willing to restore the young  woman's life on the condition that  wanted to feat the 16 colossi that  inhabit the Forbidden Land who waiter  and producer Kenji Kido held the team to  an incredibly high standard throughout  production on Shadow of the Colossus a  waiter has stated that he felt only two  out of the 500 artists who applied met  his perfectionist criteria and he would  often demand changes in design to fall  more in line with his vision likewise  Kato a veteran game designer who worked  on the original Ape Escape challenged  the programmers to implement realistic  physics and effects that would shift the  lead characters interaction  realistically in reaction to the colossi  for example if a colossus extended its  arm horizontally Kato insisted that one  to be able to run across the limb as if  he were traversing any other flat  surface the waiter again implemented his  theory of subtraction design across all  elements of the game there are no  enemies outside of the sixteen colossi  and no other life inhabits the Forbidden  Land say for the occasional white or  black tailed lizard while traversing the  flat desolate landscape only the sounds  of wander aggro and the landscape itself  can be heard with the spice use of music  search for emotional or pivotal  narrative moments the lonely hero  atmosphere epic multi-staged colossi  battles and the tragic open-ended story  of Shadow of the Colossus again proved a  critical hit for Team Ico with game  spots Brad shoemaker awarding the game  an eight point seven and surmising  there's never really been anything like  it on the PlayStation 2 or any other  platformer in stark contrast to ICO  Shadow of the Colossus was also a  commercial success selling a hundred and  forty thousand copies in its first week  in Japan almost 80% of which was in the  first two days the game didn't escape  criticism however with many reviewers  struggling with the game's erratic  framerate and camera controls a grow  also proved divisive as a waiter  intentionally had the horse ignore  players commands in some situations to  better emulate the behavior of a real  animal one thing away they never  predicted was the emotional bond players  made with Agra  during their long rides across the  Forbidden Lands he had an idea to take  that bond of a boy and his pet and  explore it in his next game project  Krakow upon completion of Shadow of the  Colossus a waiter contemplated the long  development time of his last two games  and decided to create something good in  a short period of time project Krakow  entered active development in 2007 for  the then one-year-old PlayStation 3 the  game was to follow many similar  narrative threads from ICO and Shadow of  the Colossus a young boy kidnapped and  awakened in a strange unfamiliar castle  comes across a chained up giant Griffon  like creature named Krakow while  resistant to the boy at first trucko  slowly begins to accept his help and  guidance and together the two set out to  escape their prison and find a way home  the core concept of the game was  intended to explore the developing  friendship between Trico and the boy as  they set out on a grand adventure by  2009 the team felt they had completed  enough of the game to allow it to be  showcased at that year's e3 under the  title The Last Guardian behind the  scenes however president of Sony  worldwide studios Shuhei Yoshida felt  development was slow he stated that the  team was struggling to meet a waiter's  vision on the PlayStation 3 hardware and  revealed the trailer released in 2009  was running at a much lower frame rate  and had been sped up in post-production  in 2011 Sony brought in help from its  internal teams to try and help Team Ico  optimize the game for the ps3 without  warning in late November of 2011 Game  Director for Matteo Aida left Sony he  cited the sense of crisis within himself  and upon leaving decided to set up a new  company gen design with several former  team ICO members but the new company was  faced with a choice start something new  or finish what they had started with The  Last Guardian ultimately a waiter opted  to maintain oversight of the project and  work alongside Sony's internal Japan  studio as a contractor as work continued  in 2012 the game's sluggish performance  on the ps3 Hardware was a continuing  cause of concern and with the launch of  the PlayStation 4 only a year away Sony  made the call to shift development to  the more powerful platform following the  switch certainly brought in even more  internal teams including ps4 lead  architect mark Cerny  to help migrate the highly customized  code across to the new platform work  progressed slowly and the Last Guardian  slowly faded from the public eye  in 2011 North American video game  retailer Game Stop cancelled all  pre-orders for the game following a  clerical error then in 2015  Sony allowed The Last Guardian trademark  to lapse in another unfortunate  bookkeeping oversight these events  coupled with the lack of any new info  from Sony outside of the occasional it's  not cancelled or workers progressing  statement led many to believe the title  would never see the light of day at e3  2015 The Last Guardian was reintroduced  at Sony's e3 conference with a confirmed  final it's definitely happening release  date of 2016 even though there wasn't a  live demo reveal on stage due to  treecko's unpredictable AI several  journalists got hands-on time with a  playable build of the game on the show  floor and confirmed it was a tangible  playable for real 100% video game that  was definitely coming out Fumito owada  has confirmed that even with all the  delays change of platforms and shifting  development teams the final game  represents his initial vision for The  Last Guardian we'll have to wait and see  if the story of troika and the boy  resonates with gamers like ICO and  Shadow of the Colossus before it but  from what we've seen so far the Last  Guardian looks like a completely  different and unique experience from any  video game released in the last eight  years  you

